  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of lifesaving Integrated Sexual and Reproductive Health and Gender Based Violence  interventions to the conflict-affected population in Cabo Delgado Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This UNFPA project provides lifesaving Integrated Sexual and Reproductive Health and Gender Based Violence interventions to the conflict-affected population in Cabo Delgado Province. Through this project, UNFPA procures and distributes dignity kits, provides GBV case management, psychosocial support, and mental health services, provides integrated Sexual Reproductive Health services including emergency obstetric surgeries, and distributes Inter-Agency reproductive health kits (IARH) in IDP sites and remote host communities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 87,518  people, including 43,749 women, 12,501 men, 28,303 children, and including 5,110 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
